---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell title="Review connection access">
<main id="main" class="invite-page consent-page"><a href="/" class="brand"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">u<span>c</span></span><span>unreel content<span class="brand-sub">THE CLIENT SPACE</span></span></a>
<section class="panel invite-card"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR WORKSPACE. YOUR PERMISSION.</span><h1>Review this<br/>connection<span>.</span></h1><p>An application is requesting access to unreel content. Nothing is connected until you review and approve the permissions below.</p>
<p id="consent-status" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking secure sign-in…</p>
<div id="consent-login" hidden><p>Use the Google or email sign-in options below, as available. You do not need to create a Clerk project or developer account.</p><div id="consent-sign-in" class="clerk-container"></div></div>
<form id="consent-form" hidden><div class="scope-box"><h2 id="consent-app"></h2><p id="consent-domain"></p><p id="consent-redirect"></p><p id="consent-tenant"></p><p id="consent-expiry"></p></div>
<fieldset><legend>Permissions</legend><p class="small">Review each permission. Write access lets the application change workspace data. Only checked permissions will be granted.</p><div id="consent-scopes"></div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Clients this application may access</legend><p class="small">Only the named clients you select are included.</p><div id="consent-clients"></div></fieldset>
<div class="scope-box"><strong>Understand the connection</strong><p>The selected application may access the data above through MCP and act with the selected permissions. Only approve an application you recognize and trust. Ask your workspace administrator to revoke the connection when it is no longer needed. Revoking access cannot undo changes or retrieve data already shared.</p><p>This screen does not grant invitations, content publishing, or administrator access.</p></div>
<div class="consent-actions"><button id="consent-approve" class="primary" type="submit">Approve selected access →</button><button id="consent-deny" class="text-button" type="button">Deny connection</button></div></form>
<button id="consent-retry" class="text-button" hidden>Check request again</button><button id="consent-signout" class="text-button" hidden>Sign out to use another account</button><a class="back-link" href="/">Leave without approving</a></section></main>
<script>import '../scripts/authorize';</script>
</Shell>
